      "weather": "Fine",
      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SUTTON BOLT (2) rocketed out of the boxes with a strong early sectional but gathered in and finished in the minors when second (20.93) at Nowra over 365m. Consistent performer from this draw with a win and three minor placings to his credit. Likely to feature again. SON OF BIANCA (5) was safely held last time out, finishing sixth at this track over 457m behind Doogie Mcgraw (26.34) in a Grade 4/5. Placed at his previous run. The form out of his last race has been franked. Must be included in calculations. SUMMER FAITH (7) showed little early speed at her last couple, the latest finishing seventh (20.88) in a Mix 2/3 at Goulburn. Form at the trip sound including six wins. The form from her last run stacks up well. Can measure up this time. PELOPONNESE (4) jumps at a shorter trip and still warrants respect.",
